  "question": {
    "text": "The half-life of a radioactive isotope is three hours. If the initial mass of the isotope were $256 \\mathrm{~g}$, the mass of it remaining undecayed after 18 hours would be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xNSeA",
      "text": "\n$8.0 \\mathrm{~g}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "V1vEh",
      "text": "\n$12.0 \\mathrm{~g}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DUxlG",
      "text": "\n$16.0 \\mathrm{~g}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2RDF5",
      "text": "\n$4.0 \\mathrm{~g}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}=3 \\mathrm{hrs}$. Initial mass $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_0\\right)=256 \\mathrm{~g}$\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{C}_0}{2^{\\mathrm{n}}}=\\frac{256}{(2)^6}=\\frac{256}{64}=4 \\mathrm{~g}$",
    "image": null
  },
